{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38145-how-to-run-scion-what-to-expect","id":38145,"title":"How to run Scion? What to expect","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-27T20:20:08-08:00","id":38145,"title":"How to run Scion? What to expect","content":"soon its going to be my first time running a game of scion, but i dont know how to run it. should it be a super heroes game? (im Using the first season of Heroes as an inspiration), something more secret and a shadow war like ? (American Gods) How do you run a campaing of Scion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T20:25:46-08:00","id":38150,"title":"","content":"Scion games can be pretty much whatever you make of them. You can run really action-heavy superhero-type campaigns involving lots of fighting monsters, rogue scions, and whatnot. You can run games that go heavy into divine politicking. It all depends on what you and your players want to do. So the first thing I'd do is to talk to your players, get some idea of what they want out of a Scion game, and make sure that your aims as ST and their aims are at least somewhat in line. Then get some idea of what kind of plot you want to have and what kind of characters they plan to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T21:34:12-08:00","id":38157,"title":"","content":"I was fortunate. I had played with my group before I ran Scion. They knew my style of play and I knew theirs. So we were able to jump into it and get going. But, you will still want to discuss things with them and help them design characters. This will help to make the game fun for you and for them in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T02:10:17-08:00","id":38640,"title":"","content":"The system doesn't work well past hero, and involves a lot of dice, too many. I know my players loved hero, but once into demigod we felt the system hardly worked at all, and by God, we turned to another system in the same setting that gave what we felt the original intent of the rules. We just glanced at the whole roll 46 dice and used a universal setting. Dexterity at high levels is just too ridiculous that the person with the high dexterity purposefully made himself someone who was too cool for combat so it could still be fun for everyone else. I love White Wolf and their games, but for some reason, Scion rules seemed to only work to a particular point. I I suggest familiarizing yourself with powerful homemade characters at higher ranks, and most of all contemplating the various knacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1836-jayna","name":"Jayna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:16:25-08:00","id":38652,"title":"","content":"guitarsniper is right. Any storyline fits. If your players already created their characters, you may want to create a campaign that suits their powers, their pantheons etc. Ultimately, Scion is a fighting game. You may always have to end up fighting a boss but it's really not necessary. I know it's like not really giving you any advice but we can't suggest one choice only. There are lots of plots depending on so many things. What I do not do with beginners is using Fate. Explaining how Magic works and Fatebinding was always tricky for me. Most of my players didn't like to deal with that at the beginning.<br /> Oh, and I usually need to come up with something that makes my players work together. They might have different goals but you'll need to give one good reason for them to work together or your players may be impossible to cooperate with other Scions. In this way, your players may care more about how to get the common mission done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:26:11-08:00","id":38656,"title":"","content":"Jayna is perfectly correct. Scion works great at Hero, but past Legend 4 the scaling of the Epic Attributes causes the system to fall apart. The writers didn't take Epic Attributes into account when designing the rest of the system (because it's just copied straight from Exalted for the most part), so once everyone is throwing around 7+ automatic successes, everything breaks. You'll need to find a way to fix that if you plan to run games into Demigod and God levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T02:54:04-08:00","id":39271,"title":"","content":"Okay, well, first, you can certainly use the show Heroes as an inspiration, but it's not really going to be about superheroes if you do, nevermind the title. :P I mean, there are basically, what, two whole acts of heroism in 23 episodes? Peter saving Claire from Sylar (it's debatable whether she was in any danger, really, considering the whole immortal regenerator thing) and flying boy sacrificing himself to bring the bomb high enough in the sky to save the city. Though I suppose you can count Hiro as a supervillain, what with the museum robbery...<br /> <br /> So not really a show about superheroes, but definitely a show about people with superpowers, which might arguably be a better inspiration for Scion. Gods and mythic personages do plenty of bickering and stuff. If players want to pursue personal goals instead of protecting the puny mortals, that certainly works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}